      "context_excerpt": "Recent results from the Green500 , a ranking of the world’s most energy-efficient supercomputers, underscore the contrast between GPUs versus CPUs. The top five performers in this industry standard benchmark were all NVIDIA GPUs, delivering an average of 70.1 gigaflops per watt. Meanwhile, the top CPU-only systems provided 15.5 flops per watt on average. This 4.5x differential between GPUs versus CPUs on energy efficiency highlights the massive TCO (total cost of ownership) advantage of moving these systems to GPUs.",
